              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "The front right side of an International eMV electric commercial truck outfitted as a utilities maintenance vehicle for Xcel Energy at the 2023 Denver Auto Show. The motor, unlike a conventional diesel engine, is located aft of the rear axle and the driveshaft is attached to its front end. The space underneath the hood at the front is occupied by various high voltage system components, and the batteries are mounted between the vehicle frame rails. The image's metadata latitude and metadata longitude are very inaccurate due to poor GPS reception inside the exhibition hall; please disregard them.",
